      "transit": "Varies — most are central or eastern Paris",
      "times": "A few times a year, announced late",
      "why": "Paris has a small circuit for this and it runs on promoters rather than venues, so the trick is following the right accounts. NSD Events Paris is the main one — they bring Indian stand-ups, singers, DJs and Bollywood names to France, and their shows are announced on Instagram before they appear anywhere else. Indian Events in Paris (IEP) covers the rest. Bolly Deewani runs Bolly Bazaar, a free Indian festival with dance, a market and a concert, each June in the 12th. For the big touring comics — Zakir Khan, Anubhav Singh Bassi, Kenny Sebastian, Vir Das — Paris usually gets one date wedged between London and Amsterdam, announced four to six weeks out and gone in days, so an alert beats a plan. BookMyShow International and Sulekha carry most diaspora shows; for Indian classical, watch the Musée Guimet auditorium and the Philharmonie.",
